        {
          "id": "/page/0/Text/1",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p block-type=\"Text\">IterFibo2(<i>n</i>): <i>prev</i> ← 1 <i>curr</i> ← 0 for <i>i</i> ← 1 to <i>n</i> <i>next</i> <sup>←</sup> <i>curr</i> + <i>prev</i> <i>prev</i> ← <i>curr</i> <i>curr</i> ← <i>next</i> return <i>curr</i></p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              193.92822341562984,
              69.88190391598388
            ],
            [
              304.322403927057,
              69.88190391598388
            ],
            [
              304.322403927057,
              165.30476295082696
            ],
            [
              193.92822341562984,
              165.30476295082696
            ]
          ],
          "bbox": [
            193.92822341562984,
            69.88190391598388,
            304.322403927057,
            165.30476295082696
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {},
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/0/Text/2",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p block-type=\"Text\">(This algorithm uses the non-standard but consistent base case <i>F</i><sup>−</sup><sup>1</sup> = 1 so that IterFibo2(0) returns the correct value 0.) Although saving space can be absolutely crucial in practice, we won't focus on space issues in this book.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              69.35494624919505,
              175.17461034045317
            ],
            [
              428.49553997223705,
              175.17461034045317
            ],
            [
              428.49553997223705,
              216.1365966796875
            ],
            [
              69.35494624919505,
              216.1365966796875
            ]
