        {
          "id": "/page/1/Text/1",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p block-type=\"Text\">(We can also derive this mutual recurrence directly from the matrix-squaring algorithm.) These recurrences translate directly into the following algorithm:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              51.79553042303533,
              72.72382421689845
            ],
            [
              411.8655088908194,
              72.72382421689845
            ],
            [
              411.8655088908194,
              98.901611328125
            ],
            [
              51.79553042303533,
              98.901611328125
            ]
          ],
          "bbox": [
            51.79553042303533,
            72.72382421689845,
            411.8655088908194,
            98.901611328125
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "2": "/page/0/SectionHeader/3"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/1/Text/2",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<blockquote><p block-type=\"Text\">〈〈<i>Compute the pair</i> <i>F</i><i>n</i>−<sup>1</sup> <i>,</i> <i>F</i><i><sup>n</sup></i> 〉〉 FastRecFibo(<i>n</i>) : if <i>n</i> = 1 return 0, 1 <i>m</i> ← b<i>n</i><i>/</i>2c <i>hprv</i>, <i>hcur</i> <sup>←</sup> FastRecFibo(<i>m</i>) 〈〈<i>F</i><i>m</i>−<sup>1</sup> <i>,</i> <i>F</i><i>m</i>〉〉 <i>prev</i> <sup>←</sup> <i>hprv</i><sup>2</sup> + <i>hcur</i><sup>2</sup> 〈〈<i>F</i>2<i>m</i>−<sup>1</sup> <i>curr</i> <sup>←</sup> <i>hcur</i>·(2 · <i>hprv</i> + <i>hcur</i>) 〈〈<i>F</i>2<i>m</i>〉〉 <i>next</i> <sup>←</sup> <i>prev</i> + <i>curr</i> 〈〈<i>F</i>2<i>m</i>+<sup>1</sup> 〉〉 if <i>n</i> is even return <i>prev</i>,<i>curr</i> else return <i>curr</i>, <i>next</i></p></blockquote>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              131.71098586300482,
              110.02359845294725
            ],
            [
              329.1522682866264,
              110.02359845294725
            ],
            [
              329.1522682866264,
              273.83245849609375
            ],
            [
              131.71098586300482,
              273.83245849609375
            ]
          ],
          "bbox": [
            131.71098586300482,
            110.02359845294725,
            329.1522682866264,
            273.83245849609375
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "2": "/page/0/SectionHeader/3"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/1/Text/3",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p block-type=\"Text\">Our standard recursion tree technique implies that this algorithm performs only <i>O</i>(log <i>n</i>) integer arithmetic operations.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              51.421039373655894,
              285.0902956614386
            ],
            [
              411.2268478369824,
              285.0902956614386
            ],
            [
              411.2268478369824,
              315.34014892578125
            ],
            [
              51.421039373655894,
              315.34014892578125
            ]
          ],
          "bbox": [
            51.421039373655894,
            285.0902956614386,
            411.2268478369824,
            315.34014892578125
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "2": "/page/0/SectionHeader/3"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/1/Text/4",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p block-type=\"Text\">This is an exponential speedup over the standard iterative algorithm, which was already an exponential speedup over our original recursive algorithm. Right?</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              51.481015361115496,
              312.59456508053734
            ],
            [
              411.80882137411305,
              312.59456508053734
            ],
            [
              411.80882137411305,
              354.19659423828125
            ],
            [
              51.481015361115496,
              354.19659423828125
            ]
          ],
          "bbox": [
            51.481015361115496,
            312.59456508053734,
            411.80882137411305,
            354.19659423828125
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "2": "/page/0/SectionHeader/3"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/1/SectionHeader/5",
          "block_type": "SectionHeader",
          "html": "<h2><b>Whoa! Not so fast!</b></h2>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              51.60859658818222,
              371.7698114959287
            ],
            [
              143.91624514756268,
              371.7698114959287
            ],
            [
              143.91624514756268,
              384.99232186992145
            ],
            [
              51.60859658818222,
              384.99232186992145
            ]
          ],
          "bbox": [
            51.60859658818222,
            371.7698114959287,
            143.91624514756268,
            384.99232186992145
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "2": "/page/1/SectionHeader/5"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/1/Text/6",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p block-type=\"Text\">Well, not exactly. Fibonacci numbers grow exponentially fast. The <i>n</i>th Fibonacci number is approximately <i>n</i> log<sup>10</sup> <i>φ</i> <sup>≈</sup> <i>n</i><i>/</i>5 decimal digits long, or <i>n</i> log<sup>2</sup> <i>φ</i> <sup>≈</sup> 2<i>n</i><i>/</i>3 bits. So we can't possibly compute <i>F</i><i><sup>n</sup></i> in logarithmic <i>time</i> — we need <i>Ω</i>(<i>n</i>) time just to write down the answer!</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              51.536444680316265,
              393.11135219520247
            ],
            [
              411.8048866473683,
              393.11135219520247
            ],
            [
              411.8048866473683,
              447.6976013183594
            ],
            [
              51.536444680316265,
              447.6976013183594
            ]
          ],
          "bbox": [
            51.536444680316265,
            393.11135219520247,
            411.8048866473683,
            447.6976013183594
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "2": "/page/1/SectionHeader/5"
          },
